 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106449 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the $31$st term of an arithmetic sequence given that the $22$nd term is $76$ and the $6$th term is $-4$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106449 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1bd11c6-80cb-5cfe-a97d-33176cbe000e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106948 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106948 #edb/ref 1061 54971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106948 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a29b3302-3991-50d4-b2af-0500a0002df1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106948 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106949 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106949 #edb/ref 1061 54972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106949 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "92c70c0d-cbf1-5b74-9421-f1cb3d0f5cd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106949 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106950 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106950 #edb/ref 1061 54976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106950 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a79b4d3e-e1aa-56c0-b927-8f3b62d26fa2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106950 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106951 #edb/ref 1061 54979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106951 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "87afd085-002a-56d2-8561-df9675f99c3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106951 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107164 #edb/ref 1064 "To find the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence given two arbitrary terms, we must usually apply the following:\n\n- The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by\n\n$$\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n$$\n\nwhere $a_n$ is the $n$th term, $a_1$ is the first term, and $d$ is the common difference.\n\n- We can find the common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence given two arbitrary terms using\n\n$$\nd = \\frac{a_m-a_k}{m-k}\n$$\n\nwhere $a_m$ is the $m$th term, and $a_k$ is the $k$th term.\n\nLet's see some examples." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107164 #edb/ref 1065 8084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107164 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d021f3a1-b263-5fc0-a08d-cdec57045fb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107164 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
